Hey...got some info on the nonames for ya.  I just happen to have my
noname motherboard here, so....

Is a 21066-equipped, baby AT-style motherboard that's basically a UDB
without most of the builtin features (no ethernet, video, sound).  Has 2
PCI slots (one long and one short), 4 ISA slots (one long, three short),
and one long shared PCI/ISA slot.  Also, does have an NCR 53C810 FAST
SCSI-2 controller built-in as well as one IDE interface (two drives max).  

Oh, also, it's known also as an AXPpci33 m/b.

I'll find other system info out if you'd like.  I know alot about
navigating DEC's docs.

C

